ider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":42.9,"pf":[],"description_full":"AECOM, together with its subsidiaries, provides professional infrastructure consulting services for governments, businesses, and organizations internationally. The company operates in three segments: Americas, International, and AECOM Capital. The company offers advisory, planning, consulting, architectural and engineering design, construction and program management services, and investment and development services to public and private clients in major end markets such as transportation, facilities, water, environmental, and energy. It is also involved in the investment and development of real estate projects. The company was formerly known as AECOM Technology Corporation and changed its name to AECOM in January 2015. AECOM was incorporated in 1980 and is headquartered in Dallas, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. W. Troy Rudd | Chairman & CEO | Age 60 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["AECOM is a large-cap industrials business with a $10.1B market cap on $15.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 8% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it, and 6% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $344M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 2 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.82\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 3.2\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 46% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4554552040072851},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.5M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2516632.95},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"AECOM $ACM Stock: Intech Investment Management LLC Reduces Holdings","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/20